{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The problem was in `bucket_of` in `repo/histogram.py`. It used plain integer division (`value // width`) and never capped the index, so a value exactly on the upper range boundary landed in bucket `n_buckets` instead of the last valid bucket `n_buckets - 1`.\n\nFor example, with width `10` and 3 buckets (covering 0–30), a value of `30` produced index `3`. `histogram_summary` in `repo/rows.py` then did `counts[3]` on a length-3 list, which caused the error and dropped that count from the chart.\n\nThe fix clamps any index `>= n_buckets` to `n_buckets - 1`, matching the docstring behavior for the top edge (and any value above the range). Interior values are unchanged.\n\nAll histogram tests pass."}]},"session_id":"be2bf354-bf23-485b-8f93-d2076f5fa9f2"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":26197,"duration_api_ms":26197,"is_error":false,"result":"Searching the codebase for histogram chart logic and last-bucket handling.\n\n\nFixing `bucket_of`: top-edge values (e.g. 30 with width 10) returned index 3 instead of clamping to the last bucket, causing index errors in `histogram_summary`.\n\n\nThe problem was in `bucket_of` in `repo/histogram.py`. It used plain integer division (`value // width`) and never capped the index, so a value exactly on the upper range boundary landed in bucket `n_buckets` instead of the last valid bucket `n_buckets - 1`.\n\nFor example, with width `10` and 3 buckets (covering 0–30), a value of `30` produced index `3`. `histogram_summary` in `repo/rows.py` then did `counts[3]` on a length-3 list, which caused the error and dropped that count from the chart.\n\nThe fix clamps any index `>= n_buckets` to `n_buckets - 1`, matching the docstring behavior for the top edge (and any value above the range). Interior values are unchanged.\n\nAll histogram tests pass.","session_id":"be2bf354-bf23-485b-8f93-d2076f5fa9f2","request_id":"b1ab0dad-3516-449f-8fc3-9c746e31d23e","usage":{"inputTokens":42421,"outputTokens":1283,"cacheReadTokens":63168,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
